<title>FRANCE: Alcatel aims to triple mobile phone sales.</title>
<headline>Alcatel aims to triple mobile phone sales.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Alcatel Alsthom's Business Systems division aims to triple mobile telephone sales in 1997 from one million units last year, unit chairman Jacques Dunogue said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Alcatel sold 500,000 in 1995 and sales were one million in 1996. Our goal in 1997 is three million, thanks to the new One Touch Pro range,&quot; he told reporters at a presentation of One Touch Go.</p>
<p>The goal was &quot;ambitious but achievable&quot;, he added.</p>
</text>
